{{Quote|I say we fight!''"<br />"''I say the Rebellion is finished!|[[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] and Nower Jebel|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
'''Nower Jebel''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[senator]] who represented the agricultural [[planet]] of [[Uyter]]<ref name="Visual Guide" /> in the [[Imperial Senate]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> in the [[Standard year|year]] [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|RO}}</ref> Jebel was secretly the [[Minister of Finance (Alliance)|Minister of Finance]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Visual Guide" /> and was present on [[Yavin 4]] in the [[Great Temple]] during the events leading up to the [[Battle of Scarif]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> During the [[Alliance High Command|High Command]] meeting,<ref name="High Command DB">{{Databank|alliance-high-command|Alliance High Command}}</ref> he was one of the [[Alliance Cabinet]] members<ref name="Visual Guide" /> who mistrusted the former criminal [[Jyn Erso]], disbelieved the existence of the [[Galactic Empire|Empire's]] planet killer [[superweapon]]&mdash;the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]&mdash;before adding that the rebellion was finished.<ref name="Rogue One" />

In the year [[5 ABY]], about a year after the Alliance reorganized into the [[New Republic]], Jebel had become a member of the new [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]] and maintained his position as Minister of Finance.<ref name="Empire's End" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Senator Nower Jebel, portrayed by [[Jonathan Aris]], is a character created and developed for the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|film]] ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Aris' involvement was first revealed and his character's name was first identified on [[July 27]], [[2015]] through his [[Wikipedia:Spotlight (Casting Services Company)|Spotlight]] page.<ref name="BBC">{{WebCite|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/entertainment-arts-33373171|text=Sherlock actor cast in new Star Wars film {{C|12:44}}|author=Lizo Mzimba|date=2015-07-27|accessdate=July 27, 2015|archivedate=20181231115820}}</ref> Jebel was first pictured in the second trailer for ''Rogue One''.<ref name="Trailer #2">{{SWYouTube|sC9abcLLQpI|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Trailer #2 (Official)|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-trailer-2}}</ref>

